            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Is it safe to use a pole saw near power lines?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                No. Keep yourself, the pole and the branch at least 10 feet from any overhead line, which is OSHA's minimum clearance for unqualified workers near lines up to 50 kilovolts. Consumer pole saws are not insulated, even with fiberglass poles. If branches are near a line, contact your utility; many trim them for free.
